# Copy this file to application-local.properties (git-ignored, project root — same
# level as this file) and fill in your own Strava API application's credentials from
# https://www.strava.com/settings/api. Loaded automatically via spring.config.import in
# application.properties; no environment variables to export, no shell to remember.
#
# This is one of two supported ways to supply these two values — the app reads
# STRAVA_CLIENT_ID/STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET from Spring's Environment regardless of source,
# so plain environment variables work exactly as well (and this file is entirely
# optional/skipped if absent). Use whichever fits your setup, e.g. env vars in CI or a
# container, this file for everyday local development.
STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET=
